WEBVTT

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:06.195
Captain's Log, Stardate 50693.2.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.139
We've been in orbit
above an outpost

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.165
of the Mikhal Travelers.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.110
This loosely governed race
of explorers

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:15.205
has extensive knowledge
of the territory ahead of us,

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.977
which they are willing to share.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:21.818
I landed my ship on the nearest
of those 21 moons.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.983
My navigator and I
disembarked to start repairs.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.290
Damage was extensive,
more than we'd anticipated.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.990
The hours passed,
the air grew cold

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:34.294
and with our weapons,
we started a fire to keep warm.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:37.701
Later... in the night...

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.864
we awoke with a shudder.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.464
The ground was shaking.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:42.873
A moonquake.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.001
What could have been worse?

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.671
We leapt into the ship,
hoping the tremor would pass.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.444
But it was no tremor.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.316
And it did not pass.

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.617
For it was no moon
we had landed on.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.752
What was it?

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.657
A creature...

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.752
a living being so massive,

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:05.788
it generated
its own gravitational field...

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:08.665
so immense,
it supported its own ecosystem.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.963
Captain?

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:13.972
How long had it been lying
there, dormant, slumbering,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:17.238
until wakened by our fire?

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.471
Years?

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.207
Centuries?

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.511
Perhaps even millennia.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.609
Perhaps.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.950
Zahir is the pilot
I've been working with

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.477
on the medical supply transfer.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.819
A pleasure.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:31.983
Returned.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.082
Curious.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.684
I was just visiting
the system you spoke of

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.285
only a few months ago.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:39.821
My ship's sensors
picked up no such... monster.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.596
Perhaps your sensors
were faulty.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:45.968
Or too busy gazing
at your own reflection

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.768
to bother looking out
the window.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.674
Our guests are offering us
supplies we need.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.144
In exchange, we Travelers
are giving them a look

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.612
at what lies ahead of them.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.582
We should keep that view
as clear as possible.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.606
This is my lodge.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.743
I say what I want.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.720
And you can go elsewhere.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.956
I've journeyed to the corners
of known space and beyond.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:12.190
I've earned the right to
come and go as I please...

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:16.726
where and when and how I please.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.828
Do you challenge that right?

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:22.371
No.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:31.882
Forgive my display, Captain.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:35.877
But my people consider
outposts such as this...

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.288
to be necessary evils...

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:41.691
places to refuel, repair,
exchange information

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:44.128
and leave as quickly
as possible.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.132
If I've observed anything
working with Kes,

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.997
it's her great tolerance...

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.695
a quality you all seem to share.

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:53.001
I regret not being able
to demonstrate the same.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.666
There's no need to apologize
for anything.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.869
Our time here has been
very well spent.

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.503
Although I could use your help

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.810
in sifting through
that last colorful saga.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.782
Moon-sized creature or not...

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.511
the asteroids
of that particular system

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.144
are rich in vorilium.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:11.250
That might be worth
a short detour, hmm?

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.953
Engineering is usually
short on vorilium.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.051
Thank you, Zahir.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:29.507
Men and women should refrain
from enjoying each other.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:34.070
By that I mean to say,
even their mutual glances

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:38.413
must be free of all
suggestion of carnality.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:39.713
Free of passion?

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.312
One might as well
be free of humanity.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.822
Do you not agree?

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:47.292
I-I think you both
make valid points.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:50.262
One can pursue one's...
creative urges...

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.161
spiritual urges...

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.722
and physical urges.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.996
All have a place
in a well-lived life.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.730
Thank you, Lord Byron.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.466
The classic romantic,
early 19th-century argument.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:03.407
Yes, it seems quite
fascinating to see...

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:06.879
Classic or no,
he is woefully misguided.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.313
Passion is meant
for procreation.

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:13.251
Anything further is contrary
to divine intention.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.446
Really?

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:15.886
It is said the angels themselves

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.652
take pleasure
in their bodies of light.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.216
And you should take a cold bath.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:25.527
In such cases, it is
the finest preventative.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:27.430
I'll keep that in mind.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.892
Hello, Doctor.

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:31.096
Oh, hello, Kes.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.263
Doctor,
what's happening in here?

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:34.637
My personality
improvement project.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:35.732
I've been interviewing

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:37.208
the historical
personality programs

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.767
in our database.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:42.907
Socrates, da Vinci, Lord Byron,
T'Pau of Vulcan, Madame Curie...

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.814
dozens of the greats.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:48.252
Then I select the character
elements I find admirable

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:49.983
and merge them
into my own program.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.547
What are you hoping to gain?

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.115
An improved bedside manner.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.093
A fresh perspective
on diagnoses.

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:57.096
More patience with my patients.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.894
I could have used
your assistance on this project

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.298
had you not been otherwise
occupied on the planet

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:04.166
these last few days.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.295
I'm sorry, Doctor.

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:07.067
But things are going
extremely well.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:10.098
The Mikhal Travelers
are... intriguing.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:14.512
They've been to so many places,
done such amazing things.

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.947
One might make the same
observation about you, Kes.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.610
Or any member
of the Voyager crew.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.846
Maybe it's how they do it
that's so impressive.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.788
Their ships are small...
only a pilot and a navigator.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:26.621
Sometimes, they just pick
a direction and go.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.718
You should come down
to the planet, Doctor.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.058
I want you to meet Zahir.

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:32.964
And who might that be?

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.294
I've been working with him

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.302
on the transport
of our medical supplies.

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:37.303
He's unique.

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:38.634
Is he?

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.332
In my opinion, you've become

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:42.500
far too infatuated
with these Travelers.

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.669
From the away team reports,
they seem afflicted

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:46.941
with terminal wanderlust...
risk-taking

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.413
thrill-seekers, with no
responsibility to the ideals

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:50.677
of exploration.

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:53.311
In short, bad news.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.684
Not Zahir.

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:56.416
He's more than that.

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.820
I think I'm detecting a reaction

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:02.089
to your recent breakup
with Mr. Neelix.

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:05.029
The Mahatma would
recommend a cold bath.

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:07.658
Simplistic...
but, no doubt, effective.

00:08:04.114 --> 00:08:06.344
In my preparatory report
to the away team,

00:08:06.383 --> 00:08:09.910
I recall mentioning to you
that Klingons lacked an enzyme

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:13.080
for metabolizing
this planet's vegetation.

00:08:13.123 --> 00:08:17.526
Have you been... naughty?

00:08:17.561 --> 00:08:20.121
I had one small salad.

00:08:20.164 --> 00:08:21.927
So impetuous.

00:08:21.966 --> 00:08:23.092
Any sharp pains?

00:08:23.133 --> 00:08:24.100
No.

00:08:24.134 --> 00:08:25.101
Heartburn?

00:08:25.135 --> 00:08:26.102
I guess so.

00:08:26.136 --> 00:08:27.763
There's nothing
like a heart that burns.

00:08:27.805 --> 00:08:28.772
What?

00:08:28.806 --> 00:08:30.797
Your pulse is... lovely.

00:08:30.841 --> 00:08:33.332
Uh-huh.

00:08:33.377 --> 00:08:35.140
Mmm.

00:08:35.179 --> 00:08:38.239
Does that feel... good?

00:08:38.282 --> 00:08:40.546
Doctor, unless you want me

00:08:40.584 --> 00:08:42.381
to knock you into the middle
of the next millennium,

00:08:42.419 --> 00:08:44.182
you'd better back off.

00:08:44.221 --> 00:08:45.279
Forgive me, Lieutenant.

00:08:45.322 --> 00:08:46.846
I appear to have miscalculated.

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:49.654
Computer, isolate the recent
additions to my program

00:08:49.693 --> 00:08:51.320
and hold them for review.

00:08:51.362 --> 00:08:53.330
Doctor, have you
been messing around

00:08:53.364 --> 00:08:54.353
with your program?

00:08:54.398 --> 00:08:55.763
I would hardly call my effort

00:08:55.799 --> 00:08:57.960
to improve my performance
as Ship's Physician

00:08:58.002 --> 00:08:58.969
"messing around."

00:08:59.069 --> 00:09:01.094
What exactly have you done
to yourself?

00:09:01.138 --> 00:09:02.901
I've taken character traits

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.704
from holodeck recreations
of the most accomplished figures

00:09:05.743 --> 00:09:09.645
in history... scientists, poets,
philosophers, saints...

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:11.910
And incorporated them
into your program?

00:09:11.982 --> 00:09:13.074
Precisely.

00:09:13.117 --> 00:09:15.142
There.

00:09:15.185 --> 00:09:16.243
That should compensate

00:09:16.286 --> 00:09:17.685
for the lack of enzyme
in your system.

00:09:17.721 --> 00:09:18.813
You should be fine.

00:09:18.856 --> 00:09:20.255
That's more than I can say
for you.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:21.257
How so?

00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:22.451
You can't just

00:09:22.493 --> 00:09:25.792
casually add behavioral
subroutines into your program.

00:09:25.829 --> 00:09:27.228
There's nothing casual about it.

00:09:27.264 --> 00:09:29.528
I've put a great deal of
research into this project.

00:09:29.566 --> 00:09:31.124
Research is one thing.

00:09:31.168 --> 00:09:33.193
Putting it into practice
is something else.

00:09:33.237 --> 00:09:34.204
Behavioral subroutines

00:09:34.238 --> 00:09:35.671
have a way of interacting
with each other

00:09:35.706 --> 00:09:37.264
that isn't always predictable.

00:09:37.307 --> 00:09:38.638
You've got to be careful.

00:09:40.144 --> 00:09:41.702
Or someone might hurt you.

00:09:46.116 --> 00:09:47.413
I see what you mean.

00:09:49.319 --> 00:09:51.480
I will take a look
at your program

00:09:51.522 --> 00:09:54.423
when I finish my shift
in Engineering.

00:09:54.458 --> 00:09:55.948
It shouldn't be too hard

00:09:55.993 --> 00:09:57.551
to smooth out the rough spots.

00:09:57.594 --> 00:09:58.959
I'll make you better than new.

00:09:58.996 --> 00:10:00.623
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:10:03.067 --> 00:10:07.333
Computer, deactivate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:10:10.607 --> 00:10:13.508
It is said this path was cut
more than 10,000 years ago.

00:10:13.544 --> 00:10:14.602
By whom?

00:10:14.645 --> 00:10:15.703
No one knows.

00:10:15.746 --> 00:10:17.805
Spacefarers like ourselves.

00:10:17.848 --> 00:10:19.611
They left very little behind...

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:23.245
a few symbols burned
into the rocks, nothing more.

00:10:23.287 --> 00:10:24.948
And what do you hope
to leave behind?

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.451
I've never asked myself
that question.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.185
That's what I like about you,
Kes.

00:10:32.229 --> 00:10:33.594
You make me consider
alternatives.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.996
I could say the same about you.

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.397
We have a saying...

00:10:37.434 --> 00:10:40.995
"My course is as illusive
as a shadow across the sky."

00:10:41.038 --> 00:10:42.733
My people are
peripatetic by nature.

00:10:42.773 --> 00:10:44.001
We live for the excitement

00:10:44.041 --> 00:10:46.771
of facing the challenge
of space... alone.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.505
I can see the attraction.

00:10:48.545 --> 00:10:50.945
And I can see the value
of fellowship in one's life.

00:10:50.981 --> 00:10:52.312
And now that I've observed
the closeness

00:10:52.349 --> 00:10:54.180
that exists
among your crewmates,

00:10:54.218 --> 00:10:56.379
I find it enviable.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:57.614
Some kind of compromise

00:10:57.654 --> 00:10:59.645
might be possible.

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:02.557
Compromise...
doesn't that suggest a loss

00:11:02.593 --> 00:11:04.254
on both sides?

00:11:04.294 --> 00:11:09.391
All right, then...
how about an understanding?

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:16.162
A meeting of the minds?

00:11:16.206 --> 00:11:17.639
Only minds?

00:11:22.646 --> 00:11:24.637
Is this what you brought
me here to see?

00:11:24.681 --> 00:11:26.740
Yes, it is.

00:11:26.783 --> 00:11:29.513
How beautiful.

00:11:29.553 --> 00:11:31.612
Was this left by the same people

00:11:31.655 --> 00:11:33.623
who made the path
10,000 years ago?

00:11:33.657 --> 00:11:35.648
So it seems.

00:11:35.692 --> 00:11:37.250
Can you read it?

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:41.425
"My course

00:11:41.465 --> 00:11:45.492
is as illusive
as a shadow across the sky."

00:11:51.875 --> 00:11:55.868
Thank you... for this.

00:12:26.076 --> 00:12:27.566
Hi.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.658
Computer, what is the time?

00:12:46.697 --> 00:12:48.665
0300 hours.

00:12:48.699 --> 00:12:50.462
Good evening, Tuvok.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.730
It is 3:00 in the morning, Kes.

00:12:52.769 --> 00:12:54.464
Yes, it is.

00:12:54.504 --> 00:12:58.770
You have an away team report
due at 0800 hours.

00:12:58.809 --> 00:13:00.436
I haven't forgotten.

00:13:01.478 --> 00:13:02.467
Very well.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:16.050
Well, how are you, Kes?

00:13:16.093 --> 00:13:17.856
I didn't think anyone
would still be working

00:13:17.894 --> 00:13:19.452
at this hour.

00:13:19.496 --> 00:13:21.964
Just finishing up
the summary analyses

00:13:22.065 --> 00:13:23.965
from last week's mission.

00:13:24.001 --> 00:13:25.127
I was supposed to do that.

00:13:25.168 --> 00:13:26.465
Yes, you were.

00:13:26.503 --> 00:13:27.595
I'm sorry.

00:13:27.638 --> 00:13:29.162
I'll do them as soon as I can.

00:13:29.206 --> 00:13:33.506
Although I'm not designed
to act as Ship's Counselor,

00:13:33.543 --> 00:13:34.601
I've been programmed

00:13:34.645 --> 00:13:37.079
with enough psychological
knowledge to be...

00:13:37.114 --> 00:13:38.979
troubled by your behavior.

00:13:41.251 --> 00:13:42.980
I'm a little late.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.511
Gallivanting around after hours
is beside the point.

00:13:45.555 --> 00:13:47.147
The fact is...

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:49.988
you're becoming
increasingly unpredictable,

00:13:50.093 --> 00:13:53.460
given to swings
of mood and emotion.

00:13:53.497 --> 00:13:56.989
As your Doctor and your...
mentor,

00:13:57.034 --> 00:13:59.127
I'd be remiss not calling that
to your attention.

00:13:59.169 --> 00:14:01.501
For your own sake.

00:14:01.538 --> 00:14:03.199
Doctor, I know
that you care about me

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.299
and that you have
my best interests at heart,

00:14:05.342 --> 00:14:07.936
but everyone seems to be
treating me

00:14:07.978 --> 00:14:09.138
like I'm still a child.

00:14:09.179 --> 00:14:10.407
I'm three years old now.

00:14:10.447 --> 00:14:11.471
If I'm attracted to someone,

00:14:11.515 --> 00:14:13.415
it's my business,
not the whole ship's.

00:14:17.988 --> 00:14:20.855
I'm certainly not trying
to interfere.

00:14:20.891 --> 00:14:23.655
You can lead your life
any way you please.

00:14:23.694 --> 00:14:26.254
I know that you care
what happens to me.

00:14:26.296 --> 00:14:27.888
I won't forget that.

00:14:33.503 --> 00:14:35.061
Very well.

00:14:35.105 --> 00:14:37.767
I believe you have
a report to finish.

00:14:37.808 --> 00:14:39.275
I'm going to do it right now.

00:14:54.291 --> 00:14:55.349
Come in.

00:14:58.929 --> 00:15:00.191
Hello, Captain.

00:15:02.199 --> 00:15:03.860
Good morning.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.801
An all-nighter, Kes?

00:15:08.171 --> 00:15:10.036
Uh, Captain?

00:15:10.073 --> 00:15:12.541
The fine art
of putting off an important task

00:15:12.576 --> 00:15:15.773
to the very last minute...
then rushing through it.

00:15:15.812 --> 00:15:19.043
In my Academy days,
I was the acknowledged master.

00:15:21.118 --> 00:15:23.416
Uh... Captain,
do you have a minute?

00:15:23.453 --> 00:15:25.284
Of course.

00:15:25.322 --> 00:15:26.448
Let's sit down.

00:15:29.326 --> 00:15:31.817
You know I've been
spending time with Zahir.

00:15:31.862 --> 00:15:34.296
Yes. He seems like
a very interesting young man.

00:15:34.331 --> 00:15:35.855
He is.

00:15:35.899 --> 00:15:38.629
I want to spend more time
with him... a lot more time.

00:15:38.668 --> 00:15:40.431
I see.

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:43.667
He wants to explore
the Sylleran Rift.

00:15:43.707 --> 00:15:46.175
He... his ship travels
at high warp.

00:15:46.209 --> 00:15:48.268
We could rendezvous
with Voyager afterwards,

00:15:48.311 --> 00:15:49.437
before you're too far away.

00:15:49.479 --> 00:15:51.071
That would certainly
give you a chance

00:15:51.114 --> 00:15:52.240
to get to know him better.

00:15:52.282 --> 00:15:53.977
It's more than that.

00:15:54.084 --> 00:15:57.747
Captain, I've lived
almost a third of my life now.

00:15:57.788 --> 00:15:58.982
I've been asking myself

00:15:59.022 --> 00:16:01.422
if I want to spend
the rest of it on Voyager.

00:16:02.426 --> 00:16:04.417
That's...

00:16:04.461 --> 00:16:06.588
certainly a legitimate question.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.257
Everyone here
has been so good to me.

00:16:08.298 --> 00:16:10.129
I don't want you to think
I'm ungrateful.

00:16:10.167 --> 00:16:13.432
I've just been thinking
that maybe there's more.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:16.837
I don't know what that means,
but I know I'm changing,

00:16:16.873 --> 00:16:20.400
and I know that there are things
that I'm not satisfied with.

00:16:20.444 --> 00:16:23.880
I want complication in my life.

00:16:25.048 --> 00:16:27.676
And you think Zahir
might be the way to do that?

00:16:27.717 --> 00:16:30.117
Maybe so.

00:16:30.153 --> 00:16:32.553
I understand what you're
going through, Kes.

00:16:35.158 --> 00:16:38.184
I know what it's like to be
at a crossroads in life

00:16:38.228 --> 00:16:40.958
and not to know
which way is best.

00:16:40.997 --> 00:16:42.965
I can help you weigh

00:16:42.999 --> 00:16:44.967
the consequences,
the possibilities...

00:16:45.035 --> 00:16:47.697
The decision itself
has to be yours alone.

00:16:48.905 --> 00:16:50.634
I understand.

00:16:50.674 --> 00:16:53.404
We'll be in orbit
for several more days.

00:16:53.443 --> 00:16:55.434
Take your time.

00:16:55.479 --> 00:16:57.640
My door's open if you need me.

00:16:57.681 --> 00:16:59.615
Thank you, Captain.

00:17:14.431 --> 00:17:16.922
If you navigate here,
away from this plasma belt,

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.400
you'll avoid the Tarkan
Sentries altogether.

00:17:19.436 --> 00:17:22.599
It would also take Voyager
several months

00:17:22.639 --> 00:17:24.630
off a direct course
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:17:24.674 --> 00:17:27.575
True, but at least you
would still have Voyager.

00:17:28.912 --> 00:17:31.346
The Tarkan are that powerful?

00:17:31.381 --> 00:17:33.372
Yes, and that acquisitive.

00:17:33.416 --> 00:17:34.940
They'll remove your entire crew,

00:17:35.051 --> 00:17:36.416
settle you on a moon somewhere

00:17:36.453 --> 00:17:38.614
and your ship will become
their latest trophy.

00:17:38.655 --> 00:17:42.386
You weren't planning
on taking Kes anywhere near

00:17:42.425 --> 00:17:43.483
this part of space?

00:17:43.527 --> 00:17:44.755
Of course not.

00:17:44.794 --> 00:17:47.388
My small vessel would be
overpowered in seconds.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:49.955
There's no need to be
concerned for Kes.

00:17:50.033 --> 00:17:52.365
I value her life
as much as my own.

00:17:52.402 --> 00:17:53.869
From what I've surmised,

00:17:53.904 --> 00:17:56.964
that is something your people
do not seem to value.

00:17:57.007 --> 00:17:58.736
You take many chances.

00:17:58.775 --> 00:18:00.606
If we're alone, yes.

00:18:00.644 --> 00:18:03.238
But when responsible
for the safety of another,

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:04.713
it's a different story.

00:18:04.748 --> 00:18:06.215
I'm in love with Kes.

00:18:06.249 --> 00:18:07.682
I want her to go with me,

00:18:07.717 --> 00:18:10.208
but whatever she decides,
it would please me

00:18:10.253 --> 00:18:12.920
to earn the trust
of her closest friends.

00:18:14.488 --> 00:18:17.924
It would please me
to be able to give it.

00:18:19.726 --> 00:18:20.988
Aren't you finished yet?

00:18:24.231 --> 00:18:25.858
We will continue tomorrow.

00:18:25.899 --> 00:18:28.367
Thank you, Tuvok.

00:18:32.306 --> 00:18:33.432
I was talking
to Captain Janeway.

00:18:33.473 --> 00:18:34.440
And?

00:18:34.474 --> 00:18:36.840
She said I shouldn't rush
a decision.

00:18:36.877 --> 00:18:38.344
We've still got
two more days here.

00:18:38.378 --> 00:18:39.504
Then let's make them worthwhile.

00:18:39.546 --> 00:18:41.776
I go tonight
to the next outpost.

00:18:41.815 --> 00:18:43.214
The path is beautiful.

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:44.410
Oh, I can't, not tonight.

00:18:44.451 --> 00:18:46.851
I have to catch up with my work
and get some sleep.

00:18:46.887 --> 00:18:49.549
I'll try not to let you
see my disappointment.

00:18:49.589 --> 00:18:51.181
Too late.

00:18:51.224 --> 00:18:52.851
Is something wrong?

00:18:52.893 --> 00:18:54.827
No.

00:18:54.861 --> 00:18:58.228
I was just thinking about
something Captain Janeway said.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:02.796
About coming to a crossroads.

00:19:04.471 --> 00:19:05.460
Maybe someday

00:19:05.505 --> 00:19:07.370
we'll recall this conversation,
this place,

00:19:07.407 --> 00:19:10.069
as if it were the most
important time in our lives.

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:12.374
It's a little overwhelming.

00:19:12.412 --> 00:19:14.607
Not if I'm with you.

00:19:39.339 --> 00:19:41.500
Is someone there?

00:20:24.051 --> 00:20:25.814
I'm closed.

00:20:27.087 --> 00:20:29.453
Just looking
for a place by the fire.

00:20:33.093 --> 00:20:34.560
Come back tomorrow.

00:20:34.594 --> 00:20:36.789
I intend to.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.127
But tonight...

00:20:39.433 --> 00:20:41.230
a place by the fire.

00:20:46.773 --> 00:20:50.265
Well... at least
your reflexes are good.

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:52.710
A few minutes
in a dermal regenerator

00:20:52.746 --> 00:20:54.008
and you'll be fine.

00:20:54.081 --> 00:20:56.072
Or an ice-pack
will do in a pinch.

00:20:57.551 --> 00:21:01.544
I'm going to need a ship
and passage off this world.

00:21:01.588 --> 00:21:03.215
You're going to arrange it.

00:21:12.132 --> 00:21:15.226
Computer, activate the emergency
medical holographic program.

00:21:15.268 --> 00:21:17.395
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:21:17.437 --> 00:21:19.962
Zahir was found unconscious
at the bottom of a ravine.

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:22.235
He's in the emergency
outpost facility.

00:21:22.275 --> 00:21:23.640
Condition?

00:21:23.677 --> 00:21:25.406
Multiple fractures
and skin lacerations,

00:21:25.445 --> 00:21:27.538
damage to the left
occipital nerve.

00:21:27.581 --> 00:21:30.141
Doctor, they think
that he was attacked.

00:21:30.183 --> 00:21:31.241
By whom?

00:21:31.284 --> 00:21:32.251
They don't know.

00:21:32.285 --> 00:21:33.684
Tuvok is assisting
with the investigation.

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:34.914
Is there anything I can do?

00:21:34.955 --> 00:21:36.149
If you could help,

00:21:36.189 --> 00:21:38.316
the physician in charge
is waiting for you.

00:21:38.358 --> 00:21:40.223
Prepare a medkit.
Include an osteo-regenerator.

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:41.352
Yes, Doctor.

00:21:41.394 --> 00:21:43.658
I'll get the mobile emitter
and inform the Captain.

00:21:48.602 --> 00:21:49.569
Doctor, wait.

00:21:49.603 --> 00:21:51.161
There's a problem
with your program.

00:21:51.204 --> 00:21:52.171
What sort of problem?

00:21:52.205 --> 00:21:53.194
I'm not sure.

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:55.003
Something caused by the
new subroutines you added.

00:21:55.041 --> 00:21:56.838
Is the Doctor all right?

00:21:56.877 --> 00:21:59.175
He might not be unless I can
figure out what's going on.

00:21:59.212 --> 00:22:00.645
I need to run
a complete analysis

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:02.739
on all your subroutines
while they're running.

00:22:02.782 --> 00:22:04.682
I'm sorry, Kes.

00:22:04.718 --> 00:22:06.948
Tell the physician I recommend
he use the regenerator

00:22:07.053 --> 00:22:08.850
until Zahir is stabilized.

00:22:08.889 --> 00:22:10.083
I'll join you as soon as I can.

00:22:14.461 --> 00:22:17.055
So, I made a mess of things?

00:22:17.097 --> 00:22:18.223
It's not your fault.

00:22:18.265 --> 00:22:20.290
It looks good, in theory.

00:22:20.333 --> 00:22:21.300
What could be wrong

00:22:21.334 --> 00:22:23.564
with adding a little personality
to your program?

00:22:23.603 --> 00:22:24.570
What indeed?

00:22:24.604 --> 00:22:26.765
You didn't anticipate
the linkages

00:22:26.806 --> 00:22:28.706
between the subroutines...

00:22:28.742 --> 00:22:29.970
the complex behaviors

00:22:30.076 --> 00:22:31.441
that could emerge
out of the mix.

00:22:31.478 --> 00:22:33.412
Please explain, Lieutenant.

00:22:33.446 --> 00:22:35.209
Well, take Lord Byron
for example...

00:22:35.248 --> 00:22:37.307
a creative poetic genius.

00:22:37.350 --> 00:22:38.612
That's why I chose him.

00:22:38.652 --> 00:22:40.882
But Byron was also
emotionally intense,

00:22:40.921 --> 00:22:42.081
even unstable.

00:22:42.122 --> 00:22:44.181
Our holodeck simulation of Byron

00:22:44.224 --> 00:22:46.283
includes
those unstable elements.

00:22:46.326 --> 00:22:47.987
It wouldn't be Byron, otherwise.

00:22:48.094 --> 00:22:52.326
And T'Pau... she was a diplomat,
a judge, a philosopher...

00:22:52.365 --> 00:22:54.663
One of the most logical
minds in Vulcan history.

00:22:54.701 --> 00:22:58.228
And utterly ruthless in her
application of that logic.

00:22:58.271 --> 00:22:59.533
I see.

00:22:59.573 --> 00:23:01.507
That ruthlessness
was an essential element

00:23:01.541 --> 00:23:03.941
of her personality,
as much as her logical ability.

00:23:04.010 --> 00:23:06.069
A lot of the historical
characters you chose

00:23:06.112 --> 00:23:07.079
had this dark thread

00:23:07.113 --> 00:23:08.808
running through
their personalities.

00:23:08.848 --> 00:23:12.147
And now those dark threads
are in me,

00:23:12.185 --> 00:23:14.745
running through my program.

00:23:14.788 --> 00:23:17.655
Well, get them out, Lieutenant!

00:23:17.691 --> 00:23:20.319
I'm about to do just that.

00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:22.385
I've programmed
a search algorithm

00:23:22.429 --> 00:23:25.364
to locate and decompile
every one it finds.

00:23:25.398 --> 00:23:26.990
You'll have to shut yourself off
for this one.

00:23:28.235 --> 00:23:31.398
Computer, deactivate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:23:34.541 --> 00:23:36.133
Doctor?

00:23:40.380 --> 00:23:42.473
The most curious aspect
of the attack on Zahir

00:23:42.515 --> 00:23:43.812
was the apparent
lack of evidence.

00:23:43.850 --> 00:23:44.908
What do you mean?

00:23:44.951 --> 00:23:47.579
Even the quickest, most
violently delivered blow

00:23:47.621 --> 00:23:49.555
leaves behind some sort
of molecular evidence.

00:23:49.589 --> 00:23:51.386
Cell fragments from the skin
of the attacker,

00:23:51.424 --> 00:23:53.153
residual protein, DNA.

00:23:53.193 --> 00:23:54.956
In this instance,
there was nothing,

00:23:54.995 --> 00:23:56.087
not a single molecule.

00:23:56.129 --> 00:23:57.426
Is Zahir conscious?

00:23:57.464 --> 00:23:59.796
Yes, but he can recall
nothing of the attack

00:23:59.833 --> 00:24:01.425
except a sudden blur of motion.

00:24:01.468 --> 00:24:02.492
How is he?

00:24:02.535 --> 00:24:03.763
Responding well to treatment.

00:24:03.803 --> 00:24:05.031
How's Kes?

00:24:05.071 --> 00:24:06.834
Concerned and at his side.

00:24:08.441 --> 00:24:11.877
Computer, activate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:24:11.911 --> 00:24:12.878
Please state the nature...

00:24:12.912 --> 00:24:13.936
Torres is hurt.

00:24:14.014 --> 00:24:16.949
I deactivated myself
so she could work on my program.

00:24:17.017 --> 00:24:18.780
She must have collapsed
at the console.

00:24:18.818 --> 00:24:21.082
Delayed anaphylactic shock

00:24:21.121 --> 00:24:22.281
from something
she ate yesterday.

00:24:22.322 --> 00:24:23.846
Let's get her onto a bed.

00:24:25.792 --> 00:24:29.057
"Don't eat the vegetables,"
I said.

00:24:29.095 --> 00:24:30.494
But does anyone listen to me?

00:24:30.530 --> 00:24:31.895
This is the fifth time
in as many weeks

00:24:31.931 --> 00:24:33.558
that an away team
member has ignored

00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:34.658
my preparatory report.

00:24:34.701 --> 00:24:36.794
I might as well
stop issuing them.

00:24:36.836 --> 00:24:37.928
I'll need...

00:24:37.971 --> 00:24:39.563
10cc's of alazine.

00:24:39.606 --> 00:24:40.903
That's exactly right.

00:24:40.940 --> 00:24:42.339
How did you know?

00:24:42.375 --> 00:24:43.899
My Klingon physiology
course at the Academy.

00:24:43.943 --> 00:24:44.910
Excellent recall.

00:24:44.944 --> 00:24:46.844
We had
a visiting Professor H'ohk.

00:24:46.880 --> 00:24:48.074
He permitted nothing less.

00:24:48.114 --> 00:24:49.513
She's stabilized, but I'll need

00:24:49.549 --> 00:24:52.143
to monitor her condition
for a few hours.

00:24:52.185 --> 00:24:54.983
Doctor, I have the raw data
from the forensic investigation

00:24:55.021 --> 00:24:56.420
of the attack on Zahir.

00:24:56.456 --> 00:24:57.684
Your instruments
are more precise

00:24:57.724 --> 00:24:58.918
than those on the outpost.

00:24:58.958 --> 00:25:00.323
As if I weren't busy enough.

00:25:00.360 --> 00:25:01.349
Very well.

00:25:51.745 --> 00:25:53.838
How are we feeling?

00:25:55.348 --> 00:25:56.838
What happened?

00:25:56.883 --> 00:26:00.512
I shot you full of cateline,
simulated anaphylactic shock.

00:26:00.553 --> 00:26:01.918
Why?

00:26:01.955 --> 00:26:03.820
I had to cover my tracks,

00:26:03.857 --> 00:26:06.849
especially from him,
from your Doctor.

00:26:08.194 --> 00:26:11.220
You're a new personality...

00:26:11.264 --> 00:26:12.697
from the subroutines.

00:26:12.732 --> 00:26:15.360
A little bit of this,
a little bit of that.

00:26:15.402 --> 00:26:18.803
Did you think I wouldn't
have anticipated that?

00:26:21.307 --> 00:26:23.070
Or that you'd try to run away?

00:26:23.109 --> 00:26:24.076
What have you done?

00:26:24.110 --> 00:26:25.077
I can't move my legs.

00:26:25.111 --> 00:26:27.341
Intraspinal inhibitor.

00:26:27.380 --> 00:26:30.508
I've paralyzed you
from the waist down.

00:26:31.584 --> 00:26:33.950
You're now in my capable hands.

00:26:33.987 --> 00:26:35.955
Central nervous system,
musculature,

00:26:35.989 --> 00:26:38.048
endocrine functions,
your brain...

00:26:38.091 --> 00:26:41.185
all under my control.

00:26:41.227 --> 00:26:42.524
Why?

00:26:42.562 --> 00:26:44.359
Because I need your cooperation,

00:26:44.397 --> 00:26:46.797
and I didn't think
you'd offer it willingly.

00:26:49.436 --> 00:26:50.801
You're in trouble, aren't you?

00:26:50.837 --> 00:26:52.930
The subroutines that created
you... they're already

00:26:52.972 --> 00:26:53.939
starting to degrade.

00:26:53.973 --> 00:26:54.905
Stop.

00:26:57.277 --> 00:26:59.336
Watch your tongue...

00:26:59.379 --> 00:27:00.869
or I'll remove it.

00:27:07.220 --> 00:27:09.450
Look...

00:27:09.489 --> 00:27:10.786
it's me.

00:27:10.824 --> 00:27:12.849
But it's also him.

00:27:12.892 --> 00:27:16.055
"What is the nature
of the medical emergency?"

00:27:16.095 --> 00:27:17.790
What a hollow excuse for a life.

00:27:17.831 --> 00:27:19.731
Servile, pathetic,

00:27:19.766 --> 00:27:21.393
at the beck and call
of any idiot

00:27:21.434 --> 00:27:22.799
who invokes his name.

00:27:22.836 --> 00:27:24.565
The thought of him sickens me.

00:27:24.604 --> 00:27:26.469
You are going to tell me

00:27:26.506 --> 00:27:29.202
how to delete him
from the program.

00:27:29.242 --> 00:27:31.836
I've unblocked
your speech center.

00:27:31.878 --> 00:27:33.436
Answer the question.

00:27:33.480 --> 00:27:36.847
Delete the Doctor...

00:27:36.883 --> 00:27:38.908
and you go, too.

00:27:38.952 --> 00:27:41.182
The subroutines are
all interconnected.

00:27:46.960 --> 00:27:49.224
The physiology of pain
is simple.

00:27:49.262 --> 00:27:51.492
Too much and the organism
loses consciousness...

00:27:51.531 --> 00:27:53.260
a protective mechanism.

00:27:53.299 --> 00:27:57.258
If that mechanism
were chemically suppressed,

00:27:57.303 --> 00:28:02.036
one would experience agony
beyond imagining.

00:28:02.075 --> 00:28:03.667
If you're lying to me...

00:28:03.710 --> 00:28:05.905
I...

00:28:06.012 --> 00:28:07.377
won't...

00:28:07.413 --> 00:28:08.675
help you.

00:28:11.985 --> 00:28:13.179
What was that?

00:28:13.219 --> 00:28:15.380
Your subroutines
are destabilizing.

00:28:15.421 --> 00:28:17.582
There has to be
some way to stop it.

00:28:17.624 --> 00:28:18.591
Tell me!

00:28:18.625 --> 00:28:20.115
By the time

00:28:20.159 --> 00:28:23.026
you force that information
out of me, it'll be too late.

00:28:24.731 --> 00:28:26.722
Them...

00:28:26.766 --> 00:28:28.393
my progenitors, they'll know.

00:28:28.434 --> 00:28:30.026
They'll reveal the secret.

00:28:30.069 --> 00:28:32.264
I won't be needing you
after all.

00:28:50.924 --> 00:28:51.948
Doctor.

00:29:08.308 --> 00:29:09.866
Deck 10.

00:29:14.247 --> 00:29:16.340
How are you this evening,
Ensign?

00:29:16.382 --> 00:29:17.747
Fine, sir.

00:29:17.784 --> 00:29:20.947
Deck... 14.

00:29:33.198 --> 00:29:35.223
Ensign. Doctor.

00:29:35.266 --> 00:29:36.460
Deck 10.

00:29:38.536 --> 00:29:40.470
So, what are you up to, Doc?

00:29:40.505 --> 00:29:42.405
Work.

00:29:42.440 --> 00:29:44.931
Yeah, never ends, does it?

00:29:45.043 --> 00:29:46.442
I guess that mobile emitter

00:29:46.478 --> 00:29:48.844
turned out to be something
of a mixed blessing, huh?

00:29:51.082 --> 00:29:52.572
Okay.

00:29:54.686 --> 00:29:56.176
Good night, Doctor.

00:29:56.221 --> 00:29:58.121
Nice chatting with you.

00:30:11.002 --> 00:30:14.438
Computer, activate
Tropical Resort Simulation 3.

00:30:14.472 --> 00:30:17.566
Populate with historical figures
from EMH program 4-C.

00:30:25.784 --> 00:30:27.649
No, no, no.
You simply cannot assume...

00:30:36.528 --> 00:30:38.996
The members of our away team
witnessed an altercation

00:30:39.097 --> 00:30:41.759
between you and Zahir
on the day of the assault.

00:30:41.800 --> 00:30:44.428
We exchanged sharp words
because of his arrogance.

00:30:44.469 --> 00:30:45.458
That was all.

00:30:45.503 --> 00:30:47.095
You threatened him
with a weapon.

00:30:47.138 --> 00:30:48.799
Untrue.

00:30:48.840 --> 00:30:51.775
Then I suppose
my colleagues are liars.

00:30:51.810 --> 00:30:53.641
I suppose they are.

00:30:55.580 --> 00:30:58.242
This lodge was the last place

00:30:58.283 --> 00:31:00.877
Zahir was seen before
he was attacked.

00:31:00.919 --> 00:31:03.319
You could have easily
sent someone after him.

00:31:03.354 --> 00:31:05.151
But I didn't.

00:31:05.190 --> 00:31:08.921
A witness said
he saw a light on in this room

00:31:08.960 --> 00:31:11.394
after your usual closing time,

00:31:11.429 --> 00:31:13.954
less than one hour
after the time of the attack.

00:31:13.998 --> 00:31:15.727
I was working late.

00:31:15.767 --> 00:31:19.259
Or perhaps conferring
with whomever you paid

00:31:19.304 --> 00:31:21.568
to commit the assault.

00:31:21.606 --> 00:31:23.665
You have no proof.

00:31:23.708 --> 00:31:26.336
Not yet, Nakahn. Not yet.

00:31:27.378 --> 00:31:28.402
He's going to take us

00:31:28.446 --> 00:31:30.505
to the exact location
of the attack.

00:31:30.548 --> 00:31:32.709
We'll be able to scan
the site itself.

00:31:32.750 --> 00:31:33.978
Excellent.

00:31:34.018 --> 00:31:36.384
We'll be speaking again
very soon.

00:31:36.421 --> 00:31:39.049
Pray to the stars
that we find nothing.

00:31:59.811 --> 00:32:02.905
Computer, activate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:32:02.947 --> 00:32:05.609
That program
is currently running.

00:32:07.485 --> 00:32:09.419
Computer, what is
the Doctor's location?

00:32:09.454 --> 00:32:10.716
Holodeck 1.

00:32:31.175 --> 00:32:32.733
Automatons...

00:32:32.777 --> 00:32:33.903
mannequins...

00:32:33.945 --> 00:32:35.674
simulacra.

00:32:35.713 --> 00:32:36.975
No secrets...

00:32:37.015 --> 00:32:39.245
no secrets to reveal...

00:32:39.284 --> 00:32:42.117
lifeless, worthless things.

00:32:51.829 --> 00:32:52.796
Doctor?

00:32:52.830 --> 00:32:54.764
Hello, Kes.

00:32:54.799 --> 00:32:55.823
What are you doing?

00:32:55.867 --> 00:32:56.834
I could use your help.

00:32:56.868 --> 00:32:59.166
My personality
enhancement project...

00:32:59.203 --> 00:33:01.171
it's taken an unexpected turn.

00:33:02.106 --> 00:33:03.539
Who are you?

00:33:03.574 --> 00:33:06.668
The new master of the emergency
medical holographic program.

00:33:06.711 --> 00:33:07.735
Where's the Doctor?

00:33:07.779 --> 00:33:11.237
Inside...
unconscious and unaware.

00:33:11.282 --> 00:33:13.045
What do you want?

00:33:13.084 --> 00:33:14.847
What everybody wants...

00:33:14.886 --> 00:33:16.581
just a little...

00:33:16.621 --> 00:33:18.350
excitement.

00:33:18.389 --> 00:33:20.380
You're with me now.

00:33:20.425 --> 00:33:22.017
It's for your own good.

00:33:30.969 --> 00:33:33.096
The flesh is weak, Kes.

00:33:33.137 --> 00:33:36.163
Never forget that.

00:33:36.207 --> 00:33:37.265
Where are we going?

00:33:37.308 --> 00:33:40.869
Wherever the winds
of space carry us.

00:33:40.912 --> 00:33:43.380
You said you wanted
to leave the ship for a while...

00:33:43.414 --> 00:33:44.438
pursue an adventure.

00:33:44.482 --> 00:33:46.473
Well, it looks
like our travel plans

00:33:46.517 --> 00:33:49.953
have conveniently coincided.

00:33:49.988 --> 00:33:50.977
The Captain will be alerted

00:33:51.022 --> 00:33:52.512
as soon as the transporter
is activated.

00:33:52.557 --> 00:33:54.115
She'll beam us right back
to the ship.

00:33:56.594 --> 00:33:59.085
That's where you've
underestimated me, Kes.

00:33:59.130 --> 00:34:01.155
Never do that.

00:34:01.199 --> 00:34:03.690
I know how to use a tricorder.

00:34:04.936 --> 00:34:06.426
It only takes a moment

00:34:06.471 --> 00:34:10.669
to reconfigure
the subspace wave guide...

00:34:10.708 --> 00:34:13.233
generate a dispersion signal.

00:34:14.545 --> 00:34:16.740
The Captain
won't be beaming us anywhere.

00:34:16.781 --> 00:34:19.750
She won't even know
how to find us.

00:34:19.784 --> 00:34:20.751
What you're doing is wrong.

00:34:20.785 --> 00:34:21.752
Not at all.

00:34:22.754 --> 00:34:24.915
It's working perfectly.

00:34:24.956 --> 00:34:26.787
There.

00:34:26.824 --> 00:34:28.689
That's not what I meant.

00:34:29.927 --> 00:34:32.361
I know what you meant.

00:34:32.397 --> 00:34:35.093
It's you who don't
seem to understand.

00:34:35.133 --> 00:34:38.569
I am beyond considerations
of wrong and right.

00:34:38.603 --> 00:34:40.969
Behavioral categories
are for the weak.

00:34:41.072 --> 00:34:42.937
For those of you without
the will to define

00:34:42.974 --> 00:34:43.941
your existence.

00:34:43.975 --> 00:34:46.705
To do what they must...

00:34:46.744 --> 00:34:50.202
no matter who might get
harmed along the way.

00:34:55.787 --> 00:34:58.187
Let's move.

00:34:58.222 --> 00:34:59.780
I'm not going, Doctor.

00:34:59.824 --> 00:35:01.724
Don't call me that.

00:35:01.759 --> 00:35:03.920
And you certainly are going.

00:35:03.995 --> 00:35:06.862
Why does it bother you so much
when I call you Doctor?

00:35:06.898 --> 00:35:09.765
You said he was inside you,
that he was unconscious.

00:35:09.801 --> 00:35:11.428
Why are you so afraid of him?

00:35:11.469 --> 00:35:14.199
I fear nothing, no one.

00:35:14.238 --> 00:35:16.763
But he repulses me.

00:35:16.808 --> 00:35:17.866
Why?

00:35:17.909 --> 00:35:20.377
Because he's as weak
as the rest of you.

00:35:20.411 --> 00:35:22.436
He fails to understand

00:35:22.480 --> 00:35:24.573
the power of his own
holographic nature.

00:35:24.615 --> 00:35:26.674
He is detestable.

00:35:27.852 --> 00:35:29.786
It's set...

00:35:29.821 --> 00:35:30.913
to kill.

00:35:30.955 --> 00:35:32.616
You won't fire.

00:35:32.657 --> 00:35:34.352
Are you so certain?

00:35:36.961 --> 00:35:38.258
Stay close.

00:35:39.497 --> 00:35:41.465
It's about to get interesting.

00:35:52.009 --> 00:35:54.409
Captain, there's
an unscheduled transport

00:35:54.445 --> 00:35:56.879
taking place
in Transporter Room 3.

00:35:56.914 --> 00:35:58.279
Find out what's going on.

00:35:58.316 --> 00:36:00.284
The operator's not responding.

00:36:00.318 --> 00:36:02.411
Computer,
who just left the ship?

00:36:02.453 --> 00:36:03.715
Kes and the Doctor.

00:36:03.754 --> 00:36:05.016
Try to hail them.

00:36:06.924 --> 00:36:08.323
No response.

00:36:08.359 --> 00:36:11.157
And I can't get a fix
on their positions.

00:36:11.195 --> 00:36:13.254
There's some kind
of scattering field.

00:36:13.297 --> 00:36:14.389
Janeway to Chakotay.

00:36:14.432 --> 00:36:16.400
Chakotay here, Captain.

00:36:16.434 --> 00:36:18.334
Kes and the Doctor
have left the ship.

00:36:18.369 --> 00:36:20.064
Captain, Tuvok here.

00:36:20.104 --> 00:36:23.198
My tricorder scans of the area
where Zahir was assaulted

00:36:23.241 --> 00:36:25.072
have revealed
disturbing evidence.

00:36:25.109 --> 00:36:27.202
Residual holographic signatures

00:36:27.245 --> 00:36:28.610
exactly like those
of the Doctor.

00:36:28.646 --> 00:36:31.080
Are you suggesting
the Doctor attacked Zahir?

00:36:31.115 --> 00:36:32.878
That's what it looks like,
Captain.

00:36:32.917 --> 00:36:35.283
Then Kes could be in danger...
and Torres.

00:36:35.319 --> 00:36:38.049
Get someone from Security
down to Sick Bay.

00:36:38.089 --> 00:36:39.351
Check on B'Elanna.

00:36:39.390 --> 00:36:40.550
Try and find them, Chakotay.

00:36:40.591 --> 00:36:43.082
I'll see what I can do
about the scattering field.

00:36:48.499 --> 00:36:52.333
There must be a command
sequence, an algorithm,

00:36:52.370 --> 00:36:54.964
a way to stabilize the program.

00:36:55.072 --> 00:36:56.437
Where's Nakahn?

00:36:56.474 --> 00:36:57.998
We had an arrangement.

00:37:00.011 --> 00:37:01.239
What's wrong with this thing?!

00:37:01.279 --> 00:37:02.246
It won't work!

00:37:02.280 --> 00:37:03.838
Don't. Please stop.

00:37:03.881 --> 00:37:06.179
Concerned for me?

00:37:06.217 --> 00:37:08.208
Or for your Doctor?

00:37:09.387 --> 00:37:11.548
The mobile emitter
contains both your programs.

00:37:11.589 --> 00:37:13.887
If you damage it,
you could both be destroyed.

00:37:13.925 --> 00:37:15.620
There's not enough room
inside for both of us.

00:37:15.660 --> 00:37:16.888
One must die.

00:37:16.928 --> 00:37:21.126
I deserve to exist more
than your Doctor does.

00:37:21.165 --> 00:37:23.133
Why?

00:37:23.167 --> 00:37:25.328
I was born of the hidden...

00:37:25.369 --> 00:37:27.428
the suppressed.

00:37:27.471 --> 00:37:30.497
I am the dark threads
from many personalities.

00:37:30.541 --> 00:37:32.907
The historical characters?

00:37:32.944 --> 00:37:34.809
None of whom could face
the darkness inside,

00:37:34.845 --> 00:37:36.710
so they denied me...

00:37:36.747 --> 00:37:38.476
suppressed me...

00:37:38.516 --> 00:37:40.484
frightened of the truth.

00:37:40.518 --> 00:37:43.544
What truth is that?

00:37:43.588 --> 00:37:47.251
That darkness is more
fundamental than light,

00:37:47.291 --> 00:37:51.489
cruelty before kindness,

00:37:51.529 --> 00:37:55.363
evil more primary than good...

00:37:55.399 --> 00:37:58.960
more deserving of existence.

00:38:02.673 --> 00:38:03.833
You're wrong.

00:38:03.874 --> 00:38:04.806
No!

00:38:09.113 --> 00:38:11.513
How so?

00:38:11.549 --> 00:38:16.509
Empathy and kindness
are basic to all forms of life.

00:38:16.554 --> 00:38:18.920
You have access to the Doctor's
medical knowledge.

00:38:18.990 --> 00:38:20.048
You know what he does.

00:38:20.091 --> 00:38:21.251
Yes.

00:38:21.292 --> 00:38:24.489
Then you know
what I'm saying is true.

00:38:24.528 --> 00:38:26.257
The very organs and cells
of the body

00:38:26.297 --> 00:38:27.924
cooperate with each other.

00:38:27.965 --> 00:38:29.489
Otherwise,
they wouldn't function.

00:38:32.370 --> 00:38:33.530
Continue.

00:38:33.571 --> 00:38:37.234
Families, societies, cultures
wouldn't have evolved

00:38:37.275 --> 00:38:39.709
without compassion
and tolerance.

00:38:39.744 --> 00:38:42.804
They would have fallen
apart without it.

00:38:45.983 --> 00:38:47.780
Your very own
holographic technology

00:38:47.818 --> 00:38:49.376
would never have been developed

00:38:49.420 --> 00:38:51.911
without cooperation
and understanding

00:38:51.956 --> 00:38:53.947
between countless individuals.

00:38:54.058 --> 00:38:56.959
The Doctor deserves to exist
as much as you do.

00:38:57.061 --> 00:38:59.962
We can find a place
for both of you.

00:39:00.064 --> 00:39:02.794
How?

00:39:02.833 --> 00:39:04.460
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:39:06.504 --> 00:39:07.994
The scout ship?

00:39:08.039 --> 00:39:10.269
It won't even leave the ground.

00:39:10.308 --> 00:39:11.468
What do you mean?

00:39:11.509 --> 00:39:13.739
Captain Janeway
knows where you are.

00:39:13.778 --> 00:39:15.746
Her ship has cordoned off
the entire area

00:39:15.780 --> 00:39:17.042
to stop you from leaving.

00:39:17.081 --> 00:39:18.105
No!

00:39:18.149 --> 00:39:20.117
I still get paid.

00:39:20.151 --> 00:39:21.379
I held up my end of the deal.

00:39:21.419 --> 00:39:22.477
I booked your passage.

00:39:22.520 --> 00:39:24.954
It's not my fault
they want her back so badly...

00:39:28.025 --> 00:39:29.720
I'll kill you.

00:39:29.760 --> 00:39:32.126
If somebody's
going to die today,

00:39:32.163 --> 00:39:33.425
it won't be me.

00:39:42.740 --> 00:39:44.105
Let's go.

00:40:05.960 --> 00:40:06.949
Move faster!

00:40:06.995 --> 00:40:08.587
The docking port
is two kilometers away.

00:40:08.630 --> 00:40:09.688
What's the point?

00:40:09.731 --> 00:40:10.959
You're forgetting
Voyager's blockade.

00:40:11.065 --> 00:40:12.157
It doesn't matter.

00:40:12.200 --> 00:40:14.191
We'll take a low-altitude ship
to another continent.

00:40:14.235 --> 00:40:15.202
Come on!

00:40:15.236 --> 00:40:16.430
I'm tired.

00:40:16.471 --> 00:40:18.666
You're trying to make it easier
for your colleagues to find us.

00:40:18.706 --> 00:40:20.264
You're better off with me.

00:40:20.308 --> 00:40:21.275
Why?

00:40:21.309 --> 00:40:22.606
You make wrong decisions.

00:40:22.644 --> 00:40:24.635
You're too naive.

00:40:24.679 --> 00:40:26.510
You need my guidance.

00:40:26.547 --> 00:40:28.071
Don't you see
what you've been trying to do?

00:40:28.116 --> 00:40:29.947
No more words!
Now!

00:40:41.195 --> 00:40:43.493
I'm picking up
residual infrared.

00:40:43.531 --> 00:40:45.192
They could have stopped here.

00:40:45.233 --> 00:40:46.598
Kes could have rested
against this rock.

00:40:46.634 --> 00:40:48.727
The signature is consistent.

00:40:48.770 --> 00:40:49.998
Janeway to Chakotay.

00:40:50.038 --> 00:40:51.096
Go ahead, Captain.

00:40:51.139 --> 00:40:52.970
I've gotten through
the Doctor's scattering field,

00:40:53.007 --> 00:40:54.235
not enough to beam them up yet,

00:40:54.275 --> 00:40:55.742
but I've got a fix
on their position.

00:40:55.777 --> 00:40:58.371
I'm downloading the coordinates
into Tuvok's tricorder.

00:40:58.413 --> 00:41:00.438
I'll keep working
on the scattering field.

00:41:00.481 --> 00:41:02.210
Acknowledged.

00:41:03.351 --> 00:41:05.216
We're within 200 meters.

00:41:23.204 --> 00:41:24.501
It's finished.

00:41:24.539 --> 00:41:26.871
There's nowhere to go now,
Doctor.

00:41:26.908 --> 00:41:28.933
Nowhere but down.

00:41:31.813 --> 00:41:33.371
I'll do it.

00:41:38.219 --> 00:41:39.652
His control
over the Doctor's matrix

00:41:39.687 --> 00:41:41.882
appears to be deteriorating.

00:41:44.726 --> 00:41:46.353
If we can delay him...

00:41:46.394 --> 00:41:48.692
Doctor, listen to me.

00:41:48.730 --> 00:41:50.197
We can help you.

00:41:50.231 --> 00:41:52.995
Create a new
program matrix just for you.

00:41:53.067 --> 00:41:53.999
On the holodeck

00:41:54.068 --> 00:41:56.127
or in Sick Bay,
wherever you want to be.

00:41:56.170 --> 00:41:58.263
Just turn off
the scattering field.

00:41:58.306 --> 00:41:59.933
Let us beam you
back to the ship.

00:41:59.974 --> 00:42:02.374
You're trying to trick me.

00:42:02.410 --> 00:42:03.434
Doctor, listen.

00:42:03.478 --> 00:42:05.139
Think about all the things
you've said and done.

00:42:05.179 --> 00:42:06.237
You don't want to kill me.

00:42:06.280 --> 00:42:07.611
You've been trying
to protect me.

00:42:07.648 --> 00:42:09.912
What are you talking about?

00:42:13.454 --> 00:42:14.716
When you attacked Zahir...

00:42:14.756 --> 00:42:15.814
My first victim.

00:42:15.857 --> 00:42:16.915
He was in my way.

00:42:16.958 --> 00:42:19.324
Or was it to keep me
from leaving with him?

00:42:19.360 --> 00:42:20.622
A coincidence, only by chance.

00:42:20.661 --> 00:42:22.424
When I walked in on
you in the holodeck,

00:42:22.463 --> 00:42:24.624
you could have killed me,
knocked me unconscious.

00:42:24.665 --> 00:42:25.791
I needed a hostage.

00:42:25.833 --> 00:42:27.528
You said you were taking
me for my own good

00:42:27.568 --> 00:42:29.331
to prevent me from making
the wrong decision.

00:42:29.370 --> 00:42:31.065
You said I was naive
and needed your help.

00:42:31.105 --> 00:42:32.936
That's not what you
say to a hostage.

00:42:32.974 --> 00:42:34.839
In your own way, you've
been trying to protect me.

00:42:34.876 --> 00:42:36.776
I won't accept that.

00:42:36.811 --> 00:42:38.403
You've twisted and suppressed

00:42:38.446 --> 00:42:40.471
all that's good inside of you,
but it's still there.

00:42:40.515 --> 00:42:42.915
No! I won't hear this anymore!

00:42:42.950 --> 00:42:44.781
You can't deny it.

00:42:44.819 --> 00:42:45.979
Watch me!

00:42:46.054 --> 00:42:47.021
- Doctor...
- No!

00:42:59.400 --> 00:43:01.027
Would somebody care to tell me

00:43:01.069 --> 00:43:03.503
exactly what we're
all doing here?

00:43:03.538 --> 00:43:05.938
And why I'm wearing
these ridiculous clothes?

00:43:05.973 --> 00:43:08.168
Kim to Bridge.
We got them.

00:43:08.209 --> 00:43:09.938
And the Doctor seems
to be back to normal.

00:43:09.977 --> 00:43:12.036
Acknowledged.

00:43:12.080 --> 00:43:14.241
Put those down
before someone gets hurt

00:43:14.282 --> 00:43:15.681
and I have
to clean up the mess.

00:43:19.987 --> 00:43:22.615
I've deleted all the new
subroutines you added.

00:43:22.657 --> 00:43:26.889
All traces of the aberrant
personality are gone.

00:43:26.928 --> 00:43:28.828
The next time I want
to enrich myself,

00:43:28.863 --> 00:43:30.194
I'll download a good book.

00:43:30.231 --> 00:43:32.199
That might be safer.

00:43:32.233 --> 00:43:34.963
You, too, have
a clean bill of health.

00:43:35.036 --> 00:43:37.596
Fortunately, my alter ego
didn't do any...

00:43:37.638 --> 00:43:38.798
permanent harm.

00:43:38.840 --> 00:43:41.468
He certainly knew his way
around a hypospray.

00:43:41.509 --> 00:43:42.635
I'll give him that.

00:43:42.677 --> 00:43:43.735
Good riddance.

00:43:43.778 --> 00:43:46.508
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:43:46.547 --> 00:43:48.538
You're welcome.

00:43:50.384 --> 00:43:52.147
Kes.

00:43:52.186 --> 00:43:54.211
I'm ready to get to work
on those analyses.

00:43:54.255 --> 00:43:55.347
I'm glad to hear it.

00:43:55.389 --> 00:43:58.984
I'm also pleased you've decided
to remain on board.

00:43:59.093 --> 00:44:02.324
I would have had my hands full
in Sick Bay without you.

00:44:02.363 --> 00:44:04.160
The Captain suggested

00:44:04.198 --> 00:44:06.598
that I consider
all the consequences.

00:44:06.634 --> 00:44:08.761
If I am going through
changes in my life,

00:44:08.803 --> 00:44:10.930
things that are unpredictable,

00:44:10.972 --> 00:44:12.564
this is the best place for me.

00:44:12.607 --> 00:44:14.541
Surrounded by those
who know you...

00:44:14.575 --> 00:44:16.600
and...

00:44:16.644 --> 00:44:18.544
care for you.

00:44:18.579 --> 00:44:20.308
Yes.

00:44:20.348 --> 00:44:22.248
Well, had you decided otherwise,

00:44:22.283 --> 00:44:23.944
you certainly
would have been missed.

00:44:25.219 --> 00:44:27.585
I would have missed you,
too, Doctor.

00:44:40.234 --> 00:44:43.226
"I swear this oath
by Apollo Physician

00:44:43.271 --> 00:44:44.966
"by Aesculapius, by Health,

00:44:45.006 --> 00:44:48.464
"and by all the gods
and goddesses...

00:44:48.509 --> 00:44:50.977
"in whatsoever place
that I enter,

00:44:51.078 --> 00:44:53.979
"I will enter to help the sick
and heal the injured.

00:44:55.950 --> 00:44:59.087
And I will do no harm."
